---
id: chicken-pork-stuffed-peppers
title: Stuffed Peppers
category: one_dish

yield:
  servings: 4
  cooked_g: 3400

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: true

---

Peel @yellow-onion{1}, cut it in quarters and purée it smooth in a #blender.

In a large bowl, mix @extra-lean-ground-chicken{1%package} and @lean-ground-pork{1%package} with the onion purée, @parboiled-rice{3/4%cup} (raw, unrinsed), @kosher-salt{1%tsp} and @black-pepper{1/2%tsp}. Knead by hand until evenly combined.

Cut the tops off @mixed-bell-peppers{6} and pull out the seeds and ribs. Fill each pepper loosely with the meat mixture, without packing it down: the rice swells as it cooks and tight peppers burst. Stand them upright, snug together, in a #large-pot.

Pour @canned-diced-tomatoes{1%package} and @chicken-broth{1%package} over and around the peppers; they should be about two-thirds covered. Neither has salt, so add another @kosher-salt{1/2%tsp} to the liquid.

Bring to a boil, then cover, lower the heat and simmer gently for ~simmer{1%hour}, until the peppers are soft and the rice in the filling is tender. Check halfway: the raw rice drinks some of the sauce, so if the liquid has dropped below half the height of the peppers, top it up with hot water. Taste the sauce at the end and adjust the salt.

Divide into 4 containers, one and a half peppers each, and spoon plenty of sauce over every portion.
